{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417092-what-are-the-local-consequences-of-suddenly-creating-large-herds-of-cattle","id":1417092,"title":"What are the local consequences of suddenly creating large herds of cattle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-06T19:58:42-07:00","id":1417092,"title":"What are the local consequences of suddenly creating large herds of cattle","content":"So let's say you're a terrestrial sorcerer, and you managed to learn a new spell, and it's pretty cool. It let's you make more animals. So you grab say, a cow bone, bury it in a plot of land, and out pops out a dozen or so smaller cows. It takes half a year for them to grow to maturity, by which means you got a dozen more cows. This applies to any kind of animal, like dogs, sheep, or goats. <br /> <br /> It's a ritual spell and you can do it, again and again, day after day. Which means that in the course of a month you can probably make a hundred or so extra cattle, ready to grow in less than a year. <br /> <br /> So what are the issues and societal implications of this? <br /> <br /> If it's too powerful, make it one mini cow a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T21:09:19-07:00","id":1417103,"title":"","content":"Alhat wants to know your location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T22:12:01-07:00","id":1417106,"title":"","content":"Among other things, cows have to have somewhere they can stand. If you don\u2019t have the rights to the land that they stand on, this could result in some disputes. <br /> <br /> And cows take quite a bit of land. Land that other people would probably have use for.<br /> <br /> Even if you <i>do</i> have that much land and absolutely no one takes issue with you using it for a herd of cattle where they might have done something more productive, the land itself may not be ideal for grazing. And while it\u2019s true that you could make some alterations, those might carry ecological impacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-07-2020, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T22:19:22-07:00","id":1417107,"title":"","content":"Excess livestock tends to get killed off. Sick livestock too.<br /> <br /> And on the economic end, if you make too many of them odds are you won't be able to turn a profit with their living expenses. It goes back to them being killed off or let loose, at which point they're a bit more like an invasive species. Whatever preys on them well will grow to excessive numbers, whatever feeds on grass or lives in the space they occupy gets rekt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T23:04:42-07:00","id":1417108,"title":"","content":"Which reminds me. A lot of cattle like sheep and goats tend to be used in places unsuitable for agriculture, aka cattle-grazing. Do they need a lot less stuff to survive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T03:48:07-07:00","id":1417121,"title":"","content":"[b]STAMPEDE!!!!!{/b]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T04:40:31-07:00","id":1417132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417092-what-are-the-local-consequences-of-suddenly-creating-large-herds-of-cattle?p=1417108#post1417108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which reminds me. A lot of cattle like sheep and goats tend to be used in places unsuitable for agriculture, aka cattle-grazing. Do they need a lot less stuff to survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. More importantly, they need a lot of stuff humans don't eat or use to make food, like grass. Cattle is machinery that pulls ploughs and turns grass into milk and beef!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T08:30:28-07:00","id":1417146,"title":"","content":"This depends in part on where you live. If you live in the north then feeding the cows becomes a lot harder, but if you manage a working or something to take care of food then you are set up for life...until some raiding party comes and slaughters everything. In the south you earn great profits...up until some raiding party comes and slaughters everything. I take it back it doesn't really matter where you are, either you run into difficulties that make the project unfeasible, your success draws more enemies than you can handle, or if you are indeed powerful enough to secure your magically growing herd of sheep a new city starts to gather around you looking for a share in the profits and your protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T00:01:51-07:00","id":1417273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417092-what-are-the-local-consequences-of-suddenly-creating-large-herds-of-cattle?p=1417108#post1417108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which reminds me. A lot of cattle like sheep and goats tend to be used in places unsuitable for agriculture, aka cattle-grazing. Do they need a lot less stuff to survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per animal? Much less.<br /> Per pound of meat? No, not really.<br /> <br /> Sheep eat ~3% of their body weight in dry matter (DM). Cows eat about 2%. But you can graze sheep on hills and crags, you don't have to call them in for milking and each sheep weighs SIGNIFICANTLY less than a cow.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest limiting the spell to only working under a full moon, and have it birth two, mundane calves (one male, one female) - no different to any other newborns of the species. So it takes a couple of years to grow beef to maturity, but each month nets you a breeding pair of whatever (or a side of beef and a heifer).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-08-2020, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T02:34:12-07:00","id":1417293,"title":"","content":"on top of what others have said, this may be an oversight, but cattle take 18-24 months before they're processed for meat, so if your spell makes them ready to go in 6 months you've tripled to quadrupled the speed of cattle ranching, and therefore the profits. It might screw with the ecological balance, but if this is your plan youre going to be using Workings to make grass more abundant/nutritious/fast growing anyway. <br /> <br /> you can hire enough day laborers for what is essentially Resources 1 and being a cattle baron is easily Resources 3 at this scale, so go to town. if this spell is widely known, than cattle become dirt cheap and are widely prevalent as a staple food of many cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T02:49:56-07:00","id":1417294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417092-what-are-the-local-consequences-of-suddenly-creating-large-herds-of-cattle?p=1417273#post1417273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest limiting the spell to only working under a full moon, and have it birth two, mundane calves (one male, one female) - no different to any other newborns of the species. So it takes a couple of years to grow beef to maturity, but each month nets you a breeding pair of whatever (or a side of beef and a heifer).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this pair well with say, Summoning the Harvest and other large-scale spells? Or am I just biased because I've never touched a cow in real life? <br /> <br /> Summoning the Harvest lets you create entire fields of crops in mere seconds. Raising the Earth's bones lets you construct houses, roads, and highways in less than a day. Death by obsidian butterflies lets you wipe out entire battalions at a time. And this spell... lets you create two calves per month?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T03:19:56-07:00","id":1417297,"title":"","content":"For one thing, Summoning the Harvest can only be used on a given field once per season, where this cattle multiplying spell was not given this limitation.<br /> <br /> (Also Raising the Earth\u2019s Bones kinda needs a big open space for you to construct on. You could build your thing out in the middle of nowhere, but then convincing people to use it will be a hard sell.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T05:27:44-07:00","id":1417309,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the ecological degradation due to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overgrazing\" target=\"_blank\">feeding</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_impact_of_meat_production\" target=\"_blank\">processing</a> these mega herds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T05:34:43-07:00","id":1417312,"title":"","content":"Thoughts<br /> <br /> - Are these animals clones? Or random copies of random animals from around the world? If clones, then it makes selective breeding *interesting* (clone up Dolly the Bull and then use as breeding stock). Potentially it also means a shift to fewer cows and many gelded bulls if you're breeding for meat (since you don't have to worry about reproduction so much), but I think spell costs would typically be against that. May also lead to a bunch of inbreeding problems etc.<br /> - could be useful for stealing particularly good breeds of horses and the like, just find or trade for a buried stud, then clone. Likewise long lost Solar improved breeds and the like (depending on caveats). Also easier to colonize islands etc (why bring cattle? Bring a tooth instead).<br /> - if it affects relative productivity of pastoral v agricultural subsistence, useful for pastoral peoples","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T05:36:27-07:00","id":1417314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417092-what-are-the-local-consequences-of-suddenly-creating-large-herds-of-cattle?p=1417312#post1417312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts<br /> <br /> - Are these animals clones? Or random copies of random animals from around the world? If clones, then it makes selective breeding *interesting* (clone up Dolly the Bull and then use as breeding stock). Potentially it also means a shift to fewer cows and many gelded bulls if you're breeding for meat (since you don't have to worry about reproduction so much), but I think spell costs would typically be against that. May also lead to a bunch of inbreeding problems etc.<br /> - could be useful for stealing particularly good breeds of horses and the like, just find or trade for a buried stud, then clone. Likewise long lost Solar improved breeds and the like (depending on caveats). Also easier to colonize islands etc (why bring cattle? Bring a tooth instead).<br /> - if it affects relative productivity of pastoral v agricultural subsistence, useful for pastoral peoples</div> </div> </div> </div>Random copies of random animals. Unless they're specially treated to have mutations, they're of average quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T14:17:43-07:00","id":1417369,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1216156-sorcery-workshop?p=1344063#post1344063\">this spell</a> I wrote a while back. In retrospect, I'm not sure if perhaps the spell should cost <i>something</i> to cast, but I suppose it's far from the most unreasonable way sorcerers can manipulate the economy, and as this thread has pointed out free cows come with plenty of other complications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417092-what-are-the-local-consequences-of-suddenly-creating-large-herds-of-cattle?p=1417146#post1417146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This depends in part on where you live. If you live in the north then feeding the cows becomes a lot harder, but if you manage a working or something to take care of food then you are set up for life...until some raiding party comes and slaughters everything. In the south you earn great profits...up until some raiding party comes and slaughters everything. I take it back it doesn't really matter where you are, either you run into difficulties that make the project unfeasible, your success draws more enemies than you can handle, or if you are indeed powerful enough to secure your magically growing herd of sheep a new city starts to gather around you looking for a share in the profits and your protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the problem with easily generated and readily visible wealth is that people will come looking to take it. Of course, a lot of interesting stories could develop out of this.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, some people would probably be leery of raiding a mysterious sorcerer who apparently conjures animals out of nothing, but that just means the enemies who do show up will be powerful and/or desperate.<br /> <br /> If you're doing this in the South, a potentially important question becomes whether Ahlat would actually accept sorcerously-generated cattle as part of a sacrifice. (Of course, since the whole point of his hecatomb policy is to encourage his worshipers to make war and <i>raid</i> cattle, the answer is probably &quot;only if the person sacrificing them stole them from someone else.&quot; On the other hand, maybe enough cattle sacrifices makes up for the deficit in war committed in his name?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}